  "query_preview": "..Overall, the forecast remains on track for today.\nThere is currently residual virga/cloud cover over Cochise\ncounty and may inhibit shower/storm develop this afternoon and\nevening for the area. CAMs like the HRRR have struggled with the\nplacement of this cloud cover, so the model may be a tad\noverdone with the strength and amount of storms that can develop\nthis afternoon and evening. This can change if the cloud cover \ncan dissipate late this morning into the early afternoon hours. \nOtherwise, there are showers attempting to develop over central \nPima county this morning that will produce minimal impacts.\nShould any storm develop, the main impacts will be strong\noutflow winds, with isolated gusts 40-60 mph, and possible\nblowing dust with the stronger storms. The best chances for\nstorms will be areas south and east of Tucson.\n\nOutside of the storm chances the main weather impact for today\nis the extreme heat. High temperatures will be 3 to 7 degrees\nabove normal today. Continue to practice heat safety such as\nremaining in air conditioning and shade when possible, avoiding\nstrenuous outdoor activities during peak heating, remaining\nhydrated, and checking on vulnerable populations.",
